      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yeah I've noticed this as well, its not just gestures, all avatar animators (including the location layer) are delayed loading for sometimes even up to a few minutes in my experience. No unusual behavior is visible in the debug menu.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-07-29T09:50:49.776Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This weird effect is seen in some heavy gaming worlds.\nFor example world \"Valkyrie Defense\", gestures are frozen for ~8 minutes! Confirmed it's local client side problem. Only Index, who has already finger tracking, has no problems.\nOther VR systems, who rely on VRChat own gesture system, are frozen.\nOnce you can use gestures, you will see others well. But players don't know well of their gestures are working, because it's local problem. Gestures are send correctly over network to others, it's more you cannot see itself.\n\nThis happens too in new horror world \"Unshattered Destination\", my gestures are frozen for some minutes.\n\nI think it happens in heavy worlds. It's just not nice to see it. You cannot write in air using own avatar pen system, because i noticed gesture system need it to toggle writing. \nYou're literally frozen for a while and cannot communicate well with others, forced to wait for minutes. That is kinda annoying for deaf and mutes.\nThe problem starts when you join the heavy world. So it's like initializing problem.\n\nHow come VRChat client has this problem? Why is gesture system not working immediately local after world loading? Can someone explain it?",
